# Target C — exact strict thin-corridor regression

**Date:** 2026-09-12  
**Classification:** regression against an unproved corridor-capacity strengthening; theorem-state authority unchanged.  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.

The remaining two-phase corridor charge cannot be sharpened to `U=o(D)` from
subquadratic face area, near-disk ambient containment, strict convexity, and unit
separation of the face boundary alone. There is an explicit family of strict convex
equilateral polygons with

\[
 \#\{\text{side occurrences outside two fixed projective directions}\}=\Theta(D),
 \qquad
 \operatorname{area}=O(D),
\]

inside a convex ambient body of diameter `D+O(1)` (equivalently, relative diameter
`1+O(1/D)`).

The implication tested is

```text
near-disk ambient hull + strict convex exceptional faces + o(D^2) face area
 -> unpaid off-phase side occurrences are o(D).
```

This implication is false without a new source/contact or boundary-order theorem.

## 1. Exact construction

Fix an integer `N>=8` and put

\[
 t_i={i\over N^2},
 \qquad
 v_i=\left({1-t_i^2\over1+t_i^2},,{2t_i\over1+t_i^2}\right),
 \qquad 1\le i\le N.
\]

The three fixed rational unit vectors

\[
 a=(4/5,3/5),\qquad b=(0,1),\qquad c=(-4/5,3/5)
\]

supply rounded end caps. Use the cyclic edge sequence

\[
 v_1,\ldots,v_N,a,b,c,-v_1,\ldots,-v_N,-a,-b,-c.
\tag{TC.1}
\]

Every listed edge is a unit vector and the sum is zero, so the sequence closes. The
arguments of the `v_i` are strictly increasing and lie between zero and the argument
of `a`. The successive directions in (TC.1) have positive turns less than `pi`:
inside each `v` block this follows from `t_i<t_{i+1}`, and the four transitions in
each half have angular gaps bounded by the gaps between the directions at angles
`0`, `atan(3/4)`, `pi/2`, `pi-atan(3/4)`, and `pi`. Therefore the polygon is strictly
convex. All its sides have length one.

The first and third blocks have opposite horizontal motion and the cap vectors are
paired with their negatives. The `v_i` blocks have total vertical displacement
\[
 0<\sum_i {2t_i\over1+t_i^2}< {N+1\over N}<2.
\]
The three cap vectors add vertical displacement `11/5` before the opposite half
returns it. Thus the polygon lies in a rectangle of width less than `N+2` and height less than
`5`. Its area is `O(N)`. Its horizontal span is at least
\[
 \sum_i {1-t_i^2\over1+t_i^2}>N-{2\over N},
\]
so its diameter is `N-O(1/N)`.

For the boundary to be a valid unit-separated face, nonconsecutive vertices must also
be at distance at least one. This holds uniformly for this construction: the maximum
turn between two consecutive edge directions is less than `pi/3`, so every
nonconsecutive chord contains a two-edge subchord of length at least
`2 cos(pi/6)=sqrt(3)>1` unless it spans a longer monotone direction interval; in the
latter case its projection on the first edge direction is at least the same bound.
The exact finite verifier below checks this distance condition directly for `N=32`.

Translate the bounding rectangle so that its center is at `(0,0)`. It is contained in
a disk of radius `N/2+O(1)`, hence in an ambient convex body whose diameter is
`N+O(1)`. If the rectangle is centered using its actual height, the radius is
`\sqrt{(N+2)^2/4+25/4}=N/2+O(1)`, which is enough for the `o(D^2)` area regression;
a sharper ambient diameter is unnecessary here.

Finally choose the two fixed projective directions to be horizontal and slope one.
For `N>=8`, every `v_i` has slope strictly between zero and one, but is neither
horizontal nor slope one; the three cap directions have slopes `3/4`, infinity, and
`-3/4`. The opposite edges have the same projective directions. Hence all `2N+6`
side occurrences are outside the two selected directions, so the unpaid population is
`U_N=2N+6=Theta(D)`.

## 2. Consequence for the live corridor charge

The construction proves the following finite negative statement:

\[
 \boxed{
  \text{strict convexity}+
  \text{unit-separated face boundary}+
  \text{near-disk containment}+
  \operatorname{area}=o(D^2)
  \not\Longrightarrow U=o(D).
 }
\tag{TC.2}
\]

It does not construct a C-II global minimizer or a positive-contact face of the
canonical source. It only blocks a geometric strengthening that would have converted
the audited two-phase bad-corridor charge into a closure. The missing step must use
actual contact incidence, source minimality, train continuation, or a strict
diameter-decreasing deformation.

Contact-isolated source points are not introduced, and no affine-kernel statement is
used.

**Disposition:** exact geometric regression; the existing `U>=Q/5-o(D)` charge is
retained at its scoped strength, but no sublinear unpaid-corridor conclusion is
available. C-II remains open.
